# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Astro project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added:** `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies
- **Updated:** pnpm-lock.yaml with new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **Modified:** `src/layouts/Layout.astro`
  - Imported the `inject` function from `@vercel/analytics`
  - Called `inject()` in the frontmatter to enable analytics tracking
  - This approach is the recommended method for Astro projects per the official documentation

### 3. Existing Configuration
- **Verified:** `astro.config.mjs` already has `webAnalytics: { enabled: true }` configured in the Vercel adapter
  - This was already present in the project configuration
  - No changes were needed to the config file

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows Vercel's official Astro-specific guidelines:
1. The `@vercel/analytics` package was installed via pnpm (the project's package manager)
2. The `inject()` function is called in the base layout file, ensuring analytics run on all pages
3. The integration works with the existing Vercel adapter configuration

## Testing & Verification

✅ **Type Check:** Passed (`pnpm run check`) - 0 errors, 0 warnings
✅ **Build Test:** Successful (`pnpm run build`) - completed in 8.83s
✅ **No Breaking Changes:** All existing functionality preserved

## Files Modified
- `example/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `example/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new package lock information
- `example/src/layouts/Layout.astro` - Added analytics injection

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, analytics data will automatically start being collected. The data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section of the project.

## Notes
- Analytics will only track data in production deployments
- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking
- The implementation is minimal and follows best practices for Astro projects
